{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_product_product_journey_d_census", "label": "D1\u2013D39 Decision Census", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/product/product-journey.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The root requirement source for Law 6 traceability, but never cite a D-decision without checking its conformance row first \u2014 D3, D4, D12, D19, D26, D33 and D38 have all been overridden."}, {"id": "docs_product_product_journey_stage_0_company_onboarding", "label": "Stage 0 \u2014 Company onboarding", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/product/product-journey.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Most B2B SaaS asks for everything up front and people abandon, so onboarding asks only the minimum to produce one real quote and collects the rest when actually needed; a demo Pune rooftop exists because new users understand the product by opening something finished."}, {"id": "docs_product_product_journey_stage_2_lead_capture", "label": "Stage 2 \u2014 Lead capture", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/product/product-journey.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The Lead Inbox is the owner's screen, not the rep's: one queue, one decision per lead \u2014 if triage takes more than three seconds per lead it will not get done."}, {"id": "docs_product_product_journey_phone_is_identity", "label": "Phone number is the identity \u2014 dedupe on capture, every channel", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/product/product-journey.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Duplicates are the one thing that kills solar CRMs: a homeowner who calls, fills a form and WhatsApps becomes three leads, three reps and three quotes for one very confused customer."}, {"id": "docs_product_product_journey_stage_4_site_survey", "label": "Stage 4 \u2014 Site survey (remote and physical modes)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/product/product-journey.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Remote survey is a competitive weapon, not a shortcut \u2014 a company that sends a design-backed proposal the same afternoon beats one booking a visit for next Tuesday, and the site visit becomes verification before installation rather than a prerequisite for quoting. Offline is the normal case for physical capture, not the edge case."}, {"id": "docs_product_product_journey_stage_5_design", "label": "Stage 5 \u2014 Design (the existing studio)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/product/product-journey.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_product_product_journey_stage_6b_proposal_builder", "label": "Stage 6B \u2014 The Proposal Builder (Path A and Path B)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/product/product-journey.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One 11-step builder serves both paths; a design pre-fills most fields, and without a design the same fields are typed or AI-filled \u2014 which is exactly why the honesty labelling rule exists for Path B."}, {"id": "docs_product_product_journey_stage_7_voice_agent_close", "label": "Stage 7 \u2014 Follow-up, the voice agent, and close", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/product/product-journey.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_product_product_journey_my_day", "label": "My Day (tasks, not KPIs)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/product/product-journey.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A rep never opens a chart to know who to call \u2014 dashboards are the owner's periodic decision tool, deliberately separate from the task-driven daily screens."}, {"id": "docs_product_product_journey_stage_8_projects_light", "label": "Stage 8 \u2014 Project management (light)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/product/product-journey.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_product_product_journey_customer_journey", "label": "The Customer's Journey C1\u2013C13 (the other side of the glass)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/product/product-journey.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The long DISCOM wait is the most under-served part of solar; the product's job is to make waiting visible and attributable, not faster."}, {"id": "docs_product_product_journey_tenant_configuration", "label": "Tenant Configuration (everything an EPC can make their own)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/product/product-journey.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_product_product_journey_agent_performance", "label": "Agent Performance (correlation, not attribution)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/product/product-journey.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_product_product_journey_d33", "label": "D33 \u2014 single customer link, accepted C&I risk", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/product/product-journey.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Anyone holding the link can tap Accept, including someone without authority to commit a \u20b992 lakh order, and view tracking cannot say which stakeholder opened it. The named-links-plus-OTP fix was later pulled into launch scope."}, {"id": "docs_product_product_journey_d38", "label": "D38 \u2014 billing & subscription deferred (SUPERSEDED)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/product/product-journey.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Its one pre-committed rule survived the reversal: never hold a customer's data hostage \u2014 read and export always work."}, {"id": "docs_product_product_journey_d39", "label": "D39 \u2014 the studio is kept and REFACTORED, not redesigned", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/product/product-journey.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The existing geometry, engineering logic and code carry over as-is; the work is restyling to the design system, adding the touch model and hardening to production \u2014 not designing it afresh."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_product_product_journey_d_census", "target": "docs_15_spec_resolutions_d_conformance_table", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/product/product-journey.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_product_product_journey_d_census", "target": "docs_product_product_journey_d33", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/product/product-journey.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_product_product_journey_d_census", "target": "docs_product_product_journey_d38", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/product/product-journey.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_product_product_journey_d_census", "target": "docs_product_product